# English translation supplement for the self-test CodeSystem.
#
# This file demonstrates a translation the IG Publisher ACTUALLY renders: the
# `description` of a CodeSystem (a resource type in the toolchain's translatable
# set — StructureDefinition / CodeSystem / Questionnaire). Verified in the
# self-test build (IG Publisher 2.2.11): on the /en/ CodeSystem page the
# description below appears in English; on /de/ it stays German.
#
# Naming (mandatory): input/translations/<lang>/<ResourceType>-<id>.po, wired via
# the `translation-sources` parameter in sushi-config.yaml. A wrong name (e.g.
# ValueSet-... or menu.po) is silently IGNORED by the Publisher.
#
# The msgid MUST match, byte for byte, the German source text in
# fsh-generated/resources/CodeSystem-selftest-palette.json (regenerate with
# `sushi .` and copy the exact string, umlauts included). msgstr is the English
# rendering. The German source is never edited by translation work — the
# supplement is purely additive.
#
# SCOPE NOTE (empirically verified on Publisher 2.2.11 — see docs/DESIGN.md and
# docs/recipes/add-translation.md): a plain `.po` supplement applied here to the
# resource-level `description`, but NOT to concept-level fields
# (`concept[n].display` / `concept[n].definition`) — those stayed German on /en/
# at both data and narrative level. CodeSystem.title likewise did not translate.
# Concept displays are localized the FHIR-native way, via a language-tagged
# `designation` in the resource, not via this supplement. Only the entry that
# actually renders is kept here, so the self-test stays an honest demonstration.

#: CodeSystem.description
msgid "Zwei beliebige Codes, damit die Selbsttest-IG eine CodeSystem-Seite rendert; kein MII-Artefakt."
msgstr "Two arbitrary codes so the self-test IG renders a CodeSystem page; not an MII artifact."
